# Line endings are decided here, not by each contributor's core.autocrlf.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF while
# the index and Linux CI keep LF. That surfaces as "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF" noise on every git command, and eventually as a diff that touches every
# line of a file nobody edited. Normalizing to LF in the repository AND in the
# working tree keeps the bytes byte-identical everywhere the code is built:
# a developer's machine, GitHub Actions and the Vercel build container.
#
# This matches what is already stored in the index, so adopting it produces no
# renormalization commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated lockfile — never hand-merge it; regenerate with npm instead.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true

# Binary assets. Declared explicitly so Git never attempts EOL conversion or a
# textual diff on brand art, catalog imagery, fonts or video.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
